  "projectUrl": "https://www.licenpro.tech/",
  "published": "2026-11-27T16:27:49.987Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.17.0 lets the app report usage, such as the AI tokens a request used, to the LicenPro usage counter.\n\n- LicenseClient.ReportUsageAsync / ReportAiUsageAsync report usage for the loaded license; LicenseClient.GetUsageAsync reads the license's totals for a period (default: this month), per meter and model. UsageReportManager does the same with an explicit license key.\n- Works with every license type. The product must allow app reporting: Dashboard > Product > Usage API > Settings (off by default). The license decides who the usage belongs to; the app cannot report for another license.\n- Each UsageEvent has an event id; sending it again is never counted twice, so retries are safe (temporary failures are retried for you).\n- Where usage must be beyond the customer's reach, keep reporting from your own server with signed requests; both land in the same counter.\n- LicenPro counts and reports; it never prices or bills.\n\nLanguages: .NET and VB.NET use this package. The native library adds lp_client_report_usage and lp_client_usage; the Python package adds LicenseClient.report_usage, report_ai_usage and usage.\n\nUpgrading from 1.8.x: also read the 1.11.0 release notes (public key built into the app, SignatureMismatch, rebuild).",
